From: Kiwibot JP5 bring-up <pedro@kiwibot.com>
Date: Wed, 3 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: tegra210_adsp: do not rename an already registered platform device

tegra210_adsp_audio_platform_probe() calls dev_set_name() on a device that
of_platform_populate() (tegra_aconnect_probe) already registered. dev_set_name()
kfree()s the old kobject name while other CPUs may still read it: bus_for_each_dev()
-> __driver_attach() -> platform_match() -> strcmp(dev_name(dev), ...). With balenaOS
udev loading modules in parallel this races at ~47 s after boot on the Kiwi Xavier
(KASAN: use-after-free in strcmp, freed by tegra210_adsp_audio_probe) and later shows up
as random heap corruption panics (__kmalloc, rw_verify_area, unregister_fair_sched_group).

Only set the name when it actually differs; the DT node is already called adsp_audio.
---
 nvidia/sound/soc/tegra-alt/tegra210_adsp_alt.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/nvidia/sound/soc/tegra-alt/tegra210_adsp_alt.c
+++ b/nvidia/sound/soc/tegra-alt/tegra210_adsp_alt.c
@@ -4478,7 +4478,10 @@
 
 	pr_info("tegra210_adsp_audio_platform_probe: platform probe started\n");
 
-	if (dev_set_name(&pdev->dev, "%s", DRV_NAME_ADSP) < 0) {
+	/* Renaming a registered device frees its old name under readers
+	 * (platform_match/strcmp): only do it if the name really differs. */
+	if (strcmp(dev_name(&pdev->dev), DRV_NAME_ADSP) &&
+	    dev_set_name(&pdev->dev, "%s", DRV_NAME_ADSP) < 0) {
 		dev_err(&pdev->dev, "error in setting adsp device name\n");
 		return -ENODEV;
 	}
